  "lines": {
    "prologue": {
      "We call it the Ring.": "pride",
      "My city.": "grief",
      "Six years ago, a man I loved like a father lost his daughter to the dark.": "grief",
      "On the night of the Black Comet, the edge of the world split open.": "shock",
      "Oswin, the Grey Lantern, held it for one night.": "passion",
      "The Crack closed to a hairline.": "dread",
      "And Oswin fell.": "shock",
      "His lantern went out.": "grief",
      "But a voice can pass through a hairline.": "dread",
      "We cannot win back the lands.": "grief",
      "We can only hold the roads until their people escape.": "passion",
      "Every road we hold will cost us a city.": "anger",
      "I am Ysolde, Queen of a city that is running out of cities.": "grief",
      "And you, Spirewright, are the last of Oswin's apprentices.": "passion",
      "Hold the road.": "command",
      "At dawn, he walked to the edge...": "grief",
      "and gave it every light he had.": "passion",
      "Before the Concord, before the Spire, before anyone kept count of the years...": "awe",
      "there were seven kingdoms.": "awe",
      "His name was Vael-Orrun, the High King.": "anger",
      "Where his armies marched, fire would not burn, and the wind lay down and died.": "dread",
      "The six hated one another.": "bitter",
      "They stood together anyway, each beside its oldest enemy, and drove him out past the edge of the stars.": "passion",
      "They could not kill him.": "dread",
      "So they locked the door with his own crown, and gave their lives to hold it.": "grief",
      "On the ruins of his city, we built Solenne.": "pride",
      "The exiled king made him a promise.": "dread",
      "It drove the six sleeping monarchs mad, and set each land against the one across from it.": "anger",
      "The High King has come back for what was his.": "shock",
      "Each had its own magic.": "awe",
      "Forge-runes and storm-songs.": "awe",
      "Root-craft and tide-memory.": "awe",
      "Stone-oaths and star-charts.": "awe",
      "The seventh kingdom studied them all.": "dread",
      "And its king wanted all of it.": "anger",
      "He learned to unmake magic.": "dread",
      "That is how the songs tell it.": "dread"
    },
    "assault_intro": {
      "Beyond the Crack, nothing is the right way up.": "dread",
      "Nhal Vorath.": "dread",
      "He built it out of everything his Unbound tore from our world.": "anger",
      "I am told the walls of Kethra are in it.": "grief",
      "And Vitrea.": "grief",
      "And our Dawn Gate.": "bitter"
    },
    "capital_prelude": {
      "Every survivor of every city was inside Solenne now.": "grief",
      "The Emberfolk with their iron pots of fire.": "tender",
      "The Galeborn and their horses.": "tender",
      "The Deepwood with their seed.": "tender",
      "Pearlhaven's children.": "tender",
      "The Stoneborn.": "tender",
      "The Veilwalkers.": "tender",
      "We had no more cities to give.": "grief",
      "For twenty-six cities we bought time with stone.": "bitter",
      "There is no more stone.": "passion",
      "There is only us.": "passion",
      "Hold this wall, and nobody has to run again.": "command",
      "...There's a light on the east road.": "whisper",
      "Does nobody else see it?": "hope"
    },
    "convergence_intro": {
      "Six lands were gone.": "grief",
      "Every Warden was free, and every horde that was left turned toward the Heartland at once.": "dread",
      "So the Wardens walked to Solenne.": "hope",
      "The Lord Marshal's army was camped at Crossmere, where every road on the Ring meets.": "anger",
      "That was where we went to meet him.": "passion",
      "They came to his feast as friends.": "dread",
      "At midnight they opened his gates.": "shock",
      "His city burned, and his wife and his son burned with it.": "grief",
      "The songs call it the Siege of Vael.": "bitter",
      "The Wardens call it the Night of Six Knives.": "whisper",
      "The songs had lied for two thousand years.": "bitter",
      "It did not change what we had to do.": "passion",
      "It only changed how it felt.": "grief"
    },
    "crossroads": {
      "He fought like the hero he had been.": "grief",
      "And when it was done, he did not run.": "bitter",
      "He walked away, the way a man walks out of a room he is finished with.": "anger",
      "In his camp we found a cage of grey light, and in it, a girl with white hair who had been gone for six years.": "shock"
    },
    "crownless_throne": {
      "He had no throne.": "dread",
      "He would not sit on anything that was not the centre of the world.": "anger",
      "Mirelle had seen a death at the end of the war.": "whisper",
      "She told me later what it was.": "tender",
      "It was the Seventh's.": "triumph"
    },
    "dawn": {
      "The Heart had reached the inner wall when the night split open in the east.": "shock",
      "He came up the road on foot.": "awe",
      "The Unbound fell still around him as he passed, the way the dead fall still at the end of a long walk.": "awe",
      "He had walked the road of the dead the whole way round the world.": "awe",
      "Every light we lost had passed him going the other way.": "grief",
      "He had kept them.": "tender",
      "He lifted the lantern to the broken frame of the Sunstone.": "hope",
      "And the sun came up over Solenne.": "triumph"
    },
    "earth_herald": {
      "Vholt Stormcrown taught Kaela to ride.": "grief",
      "When his thunderbird fell, she was the one waiting at the bottom of the canyon.": "grief",
      "Behind a collapsed terrace we found what was left of the Canyon's shield-company.": "dread",
      "One of them was still standing, holding a door.": "pride"
    },
    "earth_intro": {
      "The Stoneborn carve their cities into the canyon walls, and they carve the faces of their kings above the doors, so the kings can watch the road forever.": "pride",
      "The Sky came down the canyon in armour, and the kings watched that, too.": "bitter"
    },
    "earth_warden": {
      "When the Mountain Titan fell, the trees on its shoulders stopped burning.": "awe",
      "The Stoneborn sealed the Deep Halls of Grundhallow with their ancestors inside.": "grief",
      "Gorrim put a new ring in his beard, and did not speak of it.": "tender"
    },
