    "epilogue": {
      "At the end, the six Wardens joined hands around him, the way they had at the beginning of the world.": "awe",
      "And Oswin set his lantern in the empty crown.": "awe",
      "We did not kill him.": "calm",
      "I do not think he could be killed.": "dread",
      "We went home to twenty-six cities of ash.": "grief",
      "Every one of their people walked back to rebuild them.": "hope",
      "That is what we fought for.": "passion",
      "Not the land.": "passion",
      "Them.": "tender",
      "I am Ysolde, Queen of Solenne.": "pride",
      "I am old now, and I have never seen a dawn since.": "grief",
      "But I have felt every one of them.": "tender",
      "He wanted the middle of the world, so we gave it to him.": "bitter",
      "Not as its king.": "passion",
      "As its light.": "triumph",
      "For a moment, in the light, he was a man again.": "awe",
      "Grey, and tired, and much younger than I had imagined.": "tender",
      "Seven crowns.": "calm",
      "One door.": "calm",
      "Thank you.": "calm"
    },
    "heart_falls": {
      "When the Sundered Heart fell, there was a man inside it.": "shock",
      "Very small, and very grey, curled around a locket.": "grief",
      "He looked at her for a long time.": "grief",
      "Then he gave her the locket, and the ash took him.": "grief",
      "I felt the sun on my face.": "awe",
      "I could not see it, but I felt it.": "tender",
      "Solenne stood.": "triumph",
      "We had spent the whole war running.": "bitter",
      "Now we went to find him.": "command"
    },
    "long_night": {
      "There was no dawn.": "dread",
      "There has not been one since.": "grief",
      "I hold court by voice now.": "calm",
      "I have learned which footsteps are good news.": "wry",
      "Out on the roads, in the dark, we kept losing cities.": "grief",
      "And we kept saving their people.": "pride",
      "It was the only thing we were still good at.": "bitter"
    },
    "lumen_gate": {
      "Prism Wastes was the last open ground before Solenne.": "dread",
      "When we left it, there was nowhere left to go back to.": "grief",
      "The Lumen Gate, the first of our six walls, fell that night.": "shock",
      "Behind it, a knight who should have died nine hundred years ago drew her sword.": "awe"
    },
    "mirror_spire": {
      "The Spire was Solenne, made wrong.": "dread",
      "Six walls of stolen stone, and on every one, a Herald we had already buried.": "anger",
