      "Now she sang them awake.": "dread",
      "Before the end, she sang something else.": "whisper",
      "In the root-halls of Elderhollow we found the archer who had held them alone for nine days.": "pride",
      "Her bow had grown leaves.": "awe"
    },
    "nature_intro": {
      "The Verdant Deep was older than the Ring.": "awe",
      "Its people lived in trees the size of towers, and they forgot nothing.": "awe",
      "Something hollow had crept in under the canopy.": "dread",
      "At night it sang.": "whisper"
    },
    "nature_warden": {
      "The Elder Broodmother fell in the oldest tree in the world.": "awe",
      "What climbed out of the grey bark was a very old woman, and she was tired.": "tender",
      "The people of Sylvanmere left by the highest branches.": "grief",
      "Sylvaine carried the seed to Solenne in her hand the whole way.": "hope"
    },
    "night_of_falling_stars": {
      "We had lost twelve cities by then.": "grief",
      "Solenne was still bright.": "pride",
      "We thought that meant something.": "bitter",
      "At midnight, the Dawn Gate opened from the inside.": "shock",
      "They were soldiers we had fed and armed.": "anger",
      "He had been keeping them in our own barracks, under our own colours.": "anger",
      "Fennick held the gate.": "passion",
      "He had a handful of half-built towers, and a hammer, and a temper.": "pride",
      "The gatehouse came down on him.": "shock",
      "He did not let go of the gate until it did.": "grief",
      "Above it all, on the Spire of Aurel, the Lord Marshal raised a blade made from a piece of our Heartstone...": "dread",
      "...and he broke the sun.": "shock",
      "The light fell on me as I ran.": "desperate",
      "It was the last thing I ever saw.": "grief",
      "Not all of the shards went with him.": "whisper",
      "One of them fell east, and did not land.": "whisper",
      "Nobody saw it but me...": "whisper",
      "and I did not know what I had seen.": "tender",
      "When the sun should have risen, it did not.": "dread",
      "That was the beginning of the Long Night.": "grief"
    },
    "regents_counsel": {
      "Every day more of them came up the roads to Solenne.": "grief",
      "We gave them the gardens, then the squares, then the halls of the palace.": "tender",
      "The Lord Marshal found room for every one of them.": "calm",
      "He was always the first at the gates, and the last to leave.": "tender",
      "I remember thinking how kind that was.": "bitter"
    },
    "solenne_falls": {
      "The inner wall broke.": "shock",
      "The Heartstone dimmed.": "dread",
      "No.": "desperate",
      "Not like this.": "desperate",
      "Not yet.": "anger",
      "Again.": "command"
    },
    "storm_herald": {
      "Gorrath the Quarried once held the Kharum Pass for a month.": "pride",
      "He carved out his own heart to hold the Rift for his new master.": "dread",
      "Out of the ridge-dust rode the Marshal of the Steppe, who had been hunted across the plateau for eleven days, and had not once ridden in the direction of retreat.": "pride"
    },
    "storm_intro": {
      "On the Thunder Steppe the sky had never once been still.": "awe",
      "The Galeborn read the storms the way we read books.": "awe",
      "Now the clouds hung motionless, and the Stone came climbing up the plateau.": "dread"
    },
    "storm_warden": {
      "When the Thunderhead broke, the sky moved again for the first time in a season.": "triumph",
      "The Galeborn wept in the rain.": "tender",
      "The Galeborn packed the Sky-Moot onto ten thousand horses and rode for Solenne.": "grief",
      "Kaela rode last.": "pride",
      "That is how she learned the word.": "wry"
    },
    "void_herald": {
      "Mother Briar was the wisest healer in the Deepwood.": "tender",
